  "brief": {
    "story": "The junction’s controller counts through four states on two bits (S1 S0): 00 red, 01 red and amber, 10 green, 11 amber, the UK sequence. Red = NOT S1 and amber = S0 are done. Green = S1 AND NOT S0 needs its AND gate fed.",
    "goal": "Wire S1 and NOT S0 into IC2’s gate 1 so each state shows the right lights.",
    "datasheet": {
      "title": "Light sequence",
      "rows": [
        [
          "00",
          "red"
        ],
        [
          "01",
          "red + amber"
        ],
        [
          "10",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "11",
          "amber"
        ],
        [
          "IC2 gate 1",
          "pins 1, 2 = columns 17, 18"
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "hints": [
    "Look down the green column of the table: green is on only in state 10, S1 on and S0 off. So green = S1 AND NOT S0.",
    "S1 is on column 3. NOT S0 comes out of IC1 on column 6. The AND gate’s inputs are columns 17 and 18.",
    "Column 3 → column 17, and column 6 → column 18."
  ],
